+# Aventix public frontend — review handoff
+
+Prepared for Abrigo. Scope: existing public pages, shared authentication UI, password recovery UI, and unauthenticated booking entry. This is a frontend review package, not a claim that live account creation, authentication, recovery, booking, or payments are operational.
+
+## 1. Implementation summary
+
+The supplied `frotend.zip` and `frotend(1).zip` are byte-for-byte identical. The implementation extends that project; it does not replace it with another app. The task document `ABRIGO-TASKS FOR THIS PROJECT(1).docx` was read, including the event details and shared login/recovery/registration requirements. Later booking/payment tasks remain outside this phase.
+
+The archive contains Next.js 16.3.8, React 19.2.8, Tailwind 3.4, TypeScript, and lucide-react. Existing App Router pages, page shell, design tokens, local images, event cards, filters, event detail sections, and event data helpers were reused. The installed Next.js routing/error-boundary documentation was checked. There was no `.git` history or backend source in the available frontend archive. The failed whole-project upload was not used.
+
+| Area | Delivered frontend behavior |
+| --- | --- |
+| Landing `/` | Existing sections retained; search sends query/location/date to Events; categories open filtered listings; event previews now use the same event data/card component as the listing; organizer CTA opens the preview route; fake auth/booking actions removed. |
+| Events `/events` | Search, native select filters, month grouping, URL-provided landing filters, empty results, clear actions, loading skeleton, existing failure boundary, and consistent clickable event cards. Search input identity/focus is retained during filtering. |
+| Event `/events/[id]` | Existing hero, media/gallery, description, schedule, venue/map when coordinates exist, organizer, selling period, prices and category states retained; related events added; event identity checked against response; ticket links preserve category. |
+| Ticket entry `/events/[id]/tickets` | Selected event/date/venue, current category prices, disabled quantity/selection controls, sign-in links, safe event/category return URL, unavailable-event/category messaging, and account-access dialog. No reservation, seat allocation, totals, checkout, or payment is created. |
+| About `/about` | Existing non-logged-in page retained and linked to the alternate Figma hero at `/about/experience`. |
+| Contact `/contact` | Existing layout retained; useful validation and FAQ disclosures; submit explicitly opens an email app, retains the draft, and never claims delivery. |
+| Login `/login` | Email/password validation, show/hide password, disabled unsupported Remember Me, forgot/register links, submitting guard, error messages, and adapter-authorized return handling. |
+| Registration `/register`, `/register/attendee` | Account-choice cards with hover/focus states; separate first/last name, email, phone, password/confirmation, terms validation and visibility controls. The outgoing payload explicitly excludes confirmation and roles. |
+| Organizer `/register/organizer` | Both Figma steps can be previewed. Fields and submission remain disabled; the modal states that no application was submitted. No organizer/admin role selection or privilege assignment. |
+| Recovery `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password` | Email request form; neutral confirmation only after a connected adapter succeeds; reset remains locked until an adapter verifies the backend-issued recovery link; matching-password validation and invalid/expired/used-link feedback; successful reset removes the used link from history and offers Login. |
+| Shared accessibility | Labels, field errors, focus outlines, skip link, mobile menu expanded state/Escape focus return, reduced-motion support, and native-dialog focus behavior. Full browser/accessibility review remains outstanding. |
