+
+Responsive Tailwind layouts adapt cards, forms, navigation and columns for smaller screens. However, desktop/tablet/mobile pixel geometry, image crops, native-dialog behavior and horizontal overflow still need real-browser verification. The font setup from the original project remains intact; no fonts or dependencies were replaced.
+
+## 4. Interaction and integration status
+
+**Working locally:** public routes and links; event search/filter/empty/clear behavior; local preview data; event identity/category preservation; form validation and visibility; error/status rendering; disabled organizer previews; mobile menu state/Escape behavior; contact email composition; recovery and login UI states when exercised with test adapters.
+
+**Not connected to a live backend:** credentials, account persistence, session restoration/logout, duplicate-email lookup, recovery email delivery/token verification/reset, authorized role-area navigation, protected booking, seat maps, reservations, or payments. Test adapters are only in the verification harness; no fake account/session/payment implementation is shipped.
+
+`src/lib/auth/client.ts` is an explicit frontend interface boundary. Its shipped value has no network methods. Valid form submissions therefore report that the service is unavailable instead of claiming success. The empty boundary is intentional; no authentication endpoints have been invented.
+
+The existing event fetch paths (`GET /events` and `GET /events/:id`) and existing `API_URL` / `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` lookup were retained. They were already present in the uploaded frontend and are not verified backend contracts. No new event endpoint was added. Responses must map to the existing `EventDetails` frontend model; `event-payload.ts` rejects malformed payloads, invalid dates/prices/media, and unknown states. The fetch layer adds a 15-second timeout and does not switch to sample success after a live request fails.
